From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmiutils: key lists, scopes, path predicates, error texts (3549)

wmiutils: key lists, scopes, path predicates, class part, error code text

IWbemPathKeyList works on the keys of the path (and of each scope): SetKey/SetKey2 (typed values stored as
WMI key text, strings quoted and escaped), GetKey/GetKey2 (apparent CIM type, value buffers), RemoveKey,
MakeSingleton (Class=@), GetInfo, GetText. IWbemPath scopes: GetScopeCount, SetScope, SetScopeFromText,
GetScope (with the scope's key list), GetScopeAsText, RemoveScope, RemoveAllScopes. CreateClassPart,
DeleteClassPart, IsRelative, IsRelativeOrChild, IsLocal, IsSameClassName. SetText rejects a modifier flag
without an accept flag and relative paths when only absolute ones are accepted, GetText(SERVER_TOO) of an
empty path is empty (these were todo_wine in the conformance tests; the marks are removed).
IWbemStatusCodeText::GetErrorCodeText returns a description for the WMI codes (and the system message for other codes).
